# Introduction

**1.1 Introduction of the System:**
The automotive repair industry is an established sector engaged in the maintenance, repair, and servicing of vehicles. It involves a variety of activities including scheduling appointments, tracking inventory like spare parts and oils, and managing customer communications. With the rise in customer demand and the volume of daily repairs, managing these activities efficiently has become a complex task. Manual tasks, such as using paper ledgers and phone calls, are generally not efficient, accurate, or timely in completing the process.

Web and mobile applications are playing an extremely powerful role in today's business world to enhance customer engagement and productivity. Customers expect a faster service process, like instant booking and real-time repair tracking. Thus, an ability to provide automation, communication, and transparency at all levels of operation is crucial.

The system “Smart Garage Hub” is a comprehensive digital platform created to offer garage administrators, mechanics, and customers a unified platform. The system is made up of appointment management, real-time inventory tracking, and instant notifications, which helps in coordinating the staff and customers effectively. The system also brings about a rise in productivity, decreases operating delay, and enhances the quality of service.

**1.1.1 Project Title:**
Smart Garage Hub - The Modern Garage Operations Platform

**1.1.2 Category:**
The integration of Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) with Customer Relationship Management (CRM) for automotive services.

**1.1.3 Overview:**
The Smart Garage Hub is the new digital platform to assist traditional mechanical workshops in becoming more modern. The system will enable garage activities with a high volume of appointments, inventory management in real-time, and live customer updates.

**1.2 Background:**
To help in the smooth operation of daily garage tasks, the program makes use of centralized databases and real-time web sockets. By providing this option online, Smart Garage Hub makes it possible for mechanics to keep an eye on their daily tasks and promptly update customers on their vehicle's status. The site has an integrated inventory module in addition to its scheduling features, allowing administrators to easily track, choose, and restock automotive parts, tires, and other repair-related items.

**1.3 The objectives of the system are:**
* **Efficient Scheduling:** To provide a dependable booking system for customers and administrators to manage daily workloads and prevent overbooking.
* **Real-Time Inventory Processing:** To provide accurate tracking of spare parts. Whenever a part is used by a mechanic, the system automatically deducts it from the database.
* **User-Friendly Interface:** Develop React-based web interfaces for effective interaction, which include service selections, digital billing, and tracking of the repair order.
* **Scalable Data Management:** To store the user, product, and appointment data, use MongoDB, which enables efficient retrieval and future scalability.
* **Cost-Effective Solution:** By making an inexpensive management tool available on standard web browsers, one can lessen the dependency on pricey, outdated desktop software.
* **Real-Time Notifications:** Use automated alerts to expedite communication and facilitate prompt updates to customers regarding their vehicle status.

**1.4 The scope of the system:**
* **Appointment Booking:** Automated evaluation of available time slots and mechanics to schedule customer drop-offs.
* **Operational Integration:** Modules with role-based management for mechanics, inventory items, and digital billing that process totals accurately.
* **User Management:** Secure features for administrators, staff, and users to register, log in, and update their passwords.
* **Scalability:** Support for integration with potential growth, to handle multiple garage branches in the future.
* **Accessibility:** A web-based platform that works on all devices (mobile, tablet, desktop) and is appropriate for both urban and rural environments with internet access.

**1.5 Structure of the System:**

**Admin:**
* Leads the product and service management across the garage.
* Ensures stock and inventory are controlled so that it manages well.
* Tracks the service and repair processes.
* Takes on the responsibility for staff management and the overall operation of the system.

**User/Customer:**
* Uses the platform by viewing the various varieties of services offered.
* Places booking requests for vehicle repairs.
* Receives order status updates in real-time.
* Helps provide various types of feedback upon completion.

**Staff / Mechanic:**
* Uses the platform to see assigned orders and tasks for the day.
* Indicates the repair status of the customer's vehicle (e.g., In Progress, Completed).
* Manages inventory by logging the parts used during a repair operation.

**1.6 Hardware/ Software requirements used for the development:**

**Hardware Requirements:**
* Memory: 4GB or more
* RAM: Minimum 8 GB 
* Storage: 10GB or more free space
* Device: Any modern smartphone, tablet, or desktop computer.

**Software Requirements:**
* Frontend Framework: React.js with Vite
* Backend Programming: Node.js, Express.js
* Database: MongoDB (NoSQL)
* Operating System: macOS / Linux / Windows
* Libraries: Socket.IO (for real-time synchronization), Chart.js (for analytics).
* Network: Must have a high-speed Internet connection for WebSocket synchronization.

