# Conclusion and Future Scope

**7.1 Conclusion:**
The Smart Garage Hub is a modernization of traditional garage operations to a high-performance, digital-first enterprise. The combination of an Express.js REST API, a powerful backend administration panel, and a sleek customer web app brings a new era of automotive technology. 

The system acts as a proof of the use of real-time telemetry (WebSockets) in the integration process. It is much more than just a booking website; it is one continuous enterprise resource planning (ERP) solution designed to streamline the customer-facing sales process and the mechanic workflow.

**7.2 Limitations:**
* **Local Hosting & Environment Configurations:** Transitioning from local development to production deployment comes with challenges, such as setting up secure domain names and SSL/TLS certificates.
* **Payment Gateways:** The checkout pipeline runs perfectly, but further integration with real-world payment gateways (like Stripe) is required for processing credit cards online.

**7.3 Future Scope:**
* **Expanded Analytics:** Managers will eventually have access to predictive demand forecasting, indicating which spare parts will be needed based on historical trends.
* **IoT OBD-II Integration:** The physical IoT sensors could be embedded via Bluetooth OBD-II scanners to automatically read vehicle diagnostic codes directly into the mechanic's dashboard, ensuring optimum repair accuracy.
